    "q-331642": {
      "dom_id": "step-q331642",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A soccer player has a $70%$ chance of scoring a goal on a penalty kick. She takes $5$ penalty shots in a row. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that she scores at most $3$ goals?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of goals scored.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ penalty shots.\n\n- The probability of scoring is $p=70%=0.7.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.7).$\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.7)^{x}(1-0.7)^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.7)^{x}(0.3)^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that she scores at most $3$ goals. This corresponds to $P(X\\le 3).$\n\nHowever, computing\n\n$$\nP(X\\le 3)=P(X=0)+P(X=1)+…+P(X=3),\n$$\n\nwill involve many computations, so let's express our answer in terms of the complement instead. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =1-P(X>3) \\\\  & =1-[P(X=4)+P(X=5)] \\\\  & =1-[(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})(0.7)^{4}(0.3)^{5-4}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5})(0.7)^{5}(0.3)^{5-5}] \\\\  & =1-[5(0.7)^{4}(0.3)+(0.7)^{5}] \\\\  & =1-0.528\\,220 \\\\  & ≈0.472,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
